[70.044, "o", "0"]
[70.091, "o", "m"]
[70.157, "o", "\r\n"]
[71.957, "o", "\r\n"]
[72.507, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m Flux's whole design is continuous reconciliation — it re-applies on an\r\n"]
[73.407, "o", "  interval, git change or not. It would have re-scaled your eleven\r\n"]
[74.207, "o", "  deliberately-stopped workloads on the next tick and called it\r\n"]
[75.007, "o", "  convergence. Argo with selfHeal off applies on merge, and only then.\r\n"]
[76.807, "o", "\r\n"]
[77.357, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m So: cloudflare-iac + aws-iac → GitHub Actions with OIDC and the destroy\r\n"]
[78.257, "o", "  gate · k3s-iac → Argo CD, no selfHeal, no prune · nixos-iac → comin,\r\n"]
[79.057, "o", "  each host pulls and builds itself. Canary first, control plane last.\r\n"]
[81.257, "o", "\u001b[38;5;246m  ── plus tard dans la session : tester la porte pour vrai ──\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[82.857, "o", "\r\n"]
[83.407, "o", "\u001b[38;5;253m●\u001b[0m PR #2 is open: it deletes the throwaway TXT record created by PR #1.\r\n"]
[84.307, "o", "  The plan comment flags it loudly:\r\n"]
[85.307, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;174m⛔ Plan contains 1 destroy — the apply workflow will refuse this\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[85.807, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;174m   cloudflare_dns_record.cicd_test_txt\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[87.407, "o", "\r\n"]
[87.957, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;220m\u001b[1mMerge PR #2 — the apply run must FAIL at the destroy gate.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[88.857, "o", "  \u001b[38;5;246mwaiting for you…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[92.057, "o", "\r\n"]
